      "voice": "Kore",
      "sectionID": "routes",
      "spokenText": "Water, soil, air and food can carry a substance. Ingestion, surface contact and transfer across respiratory surfaces describe receptor-specific routes of contact or entry. Two organisms in the same medium may experience different routes and amounts. A water concentration in mg/L does not become an organism's dose without further data and a model. Timing matters. A post-rain water sample describes a different moment from a pre-event sample. An application record may establish an activity, but not the concentration reaching a stream. Sampling times, locations and comparisons must fit the question, with appropriate analytical and sampling quality checks.",
